By the Pythagorean theorem, $w - C = M$.

But $w$ is also the projection of $C$ onto the line connecting $c$ and $z$, so $w - C = \frac{2}{4} (z - c)$.

Then $w = C + \frac{1}{4} (z - c) = (2,-3) + \frac{1}{4} (2 - \sqrt{2} + 3 \sqrt{2} - 2 + 3i) = \boxed{3 + \sqrt{2}}.$
[asy]
unitsize(0.6 cm);

pair C, W, Z;

Z = (2 + sqrt(2), -3 - 3*sqrt(2));
C = (2,-3);
W = rotate(45,C)*(Z);

draw(Z--C--W);

dot("$c$", C, N);
dot
